1
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:06,401
[This drama is intended for entertainment purposes only.]

2
00:00:06,411 --> 00:00:08,400
[All characters, behaviors, locations, and events depicted are fictional.]

3
00:00:08,430 --> 00:00:09,950
[It is not intended to be sexually suggestive or to encourage viewers]

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,501
[to engage in inappropriate or morally objectionable behavior.]

5
00:00:11,511 --> 00:00:12,890
[Nor is it intended to discredit any profession]

6
00:00:12,899 --> 00:00:13,900
[or create negative perceptions of any organization]

7
00:00:13,911 --> 00:00:14,912
[or any particular group of people.]

8
00:00:15,051 --> 00:00:16,160
I've got some intel.

9
00:00:16,946 --> 00:00:19,000
Ta and the Director have built a house in Khao Yai.

10
00:00:19,067 --> 00:00:20,800
They're planning to run away and live together.

11
00:00:20,995 --> 00:00:21,996
Answer me!

12
00:00:22,264 --> 00:00:23,960
- Are you moving in with her?
- Damn right!

13
00:00:24,291 --> 00:00:25,840
And I'm taking Titus with me!

14
00:00:25,998 --> 00:00:28,000
So she won't grow up to be a complete lunatic like you!

15
00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:32,560
Wow, people on social media are so quick, Ta.

16
00:00:32,678 --> 00:00:35,720
You sent that video to provoke Nopnapha at just the right moment.

17
00:00:35,907 --> 00:00:38,638
Wow, that plot of land is beautiful. Where is it?

18
00:00:38,926 --> 00:00:41,120
That land belongs to Mutta.

19
00:00:41,179 --> 00:00:43,280
And that house is hers, too. It was just built.

20
00:00:43,382 --> 00:00:45,216
If she's got that much money,

21
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:47,640
why is she still leeching off Jenphop?

22
00:00:47,678 --> 00:00:49,880
Or does she really love Phop?

23
00:00:50,947 --> 00:00:53,200
Let's stop making each other miserable, Napha.

24
00:00:53,920 --> 00:00:54,921
Let's get a divorce.

25
00:00:55,928 --> 00:00:57,560
I've already told Nopnapha I want a divorce.

26
00:00:57,656 --> 00:00:59,157
I'm just waiting for her to set a date to sign the papers.

27
00:00:59,208 --> 00:01:01,000
Stay here with me and get away from it all for a while, Ta.

28
00:01:01,126 --> 00:01:04,240
The airline confirmed that Mr. Jenphop and that Mutta

29
00:01:04,331 --> 00:01:05,840
flew to Chiang Mai, ma'am.

30
00:01:05,904 --> 00:01:08,520
Since I've been suspended from my duties anyway,

31
00:01:08,656 --> 00:01:11,320
might as well make the most of my time off by slapping that mistress around!

32
00:01:20,416 --> 00:01:23,480
Where is our room?

33
00:01:26,451 --> 00:01:27,452
Okay.

34
00:01:30,206 --> 00:01:31,207
Let's go.

35
00:01:36,683 --> 00:01:37,684
Wow!

36
00:01:46,494 --> 00:01:49,680
Who would've thought things would come to this?

37
00:01:53,678 --> 00:01:55,520
If only I'd been more firm back then

38
00:01:56,104 --> 00:01:58,280
and told Nopnapha to get an abortion so we could go our separate ways,

39
00:01:59,363 --> 00:02:01,560
I wouldn't be sitting here worrying like this.

40
00:02:02,883 --> 00:02:04,680
But then you wouldn't have become a director.

41
00:02:07,731 --> 00:02:09,507
I overheard some people in your department gossiping.

42
00:02:09,731 --> 00:02:13,040
They said you only became a director because of your wife's influence.

43
00:02:19,731 --> 00:02:20,960
Well, they're not wrong.

44
00:02:25,350 --> 00:02:27,360
But marrying Nopnapha did have its good sides.

45
00:02:28,614 --> 00:02:31,760
And the best thing was having our two children.

46
00:02:32,752 --> 00:02:34,155
They may be stubborn sometimes,

47
00:02:35,414 --> 00:02:36,415
but...

48
00:02:39,648 --> 00:02:41,718
they've taught me what it means to be a father.

49
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:44,640
Some people might think

50
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:47,601
I've stayed with Nopnapha

51
00:02:49,254 --> 00:02:50,640
because I want to live off her money

52
00:02:51,888 --> 00:02:53,000
or advance my career.

53
00:02:55,686 --> 00:02:56,725
But the truth is,

54
00:02:59,371 --> 00:03:01,040
my children are the main reason I've stayed.

55
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:04,960
And after the divorce,

56
00:03:06,494 --> 00:03:07,560
what will happen with the children?

57
00:03:09,475 --> 00:03:10,760
We'll probably have to fight it out in court.

58
00:03:12,227 --> 00:03:13,880
I want the children to live with me.

59
00:03:15,384 --> 00:03:17,240
Even if I only get custody of Titus, that would be something.

60
00:03:19,752 --> 00:03:22,960
You're such a loving father, Jenphop.

61
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:26,441
Tetris and Titus are so lucky.

62
00:03:28,987 --> 00:03:31,024
If I hadn't lost my baby,

63
00:03:33,179 --> 00:03:34,840
our child would've been just as lucky.

64
00:03:36,598 --> 00:03:37,599
Jenphop.

65
00:03:40,059 --> 00:03:41,520
Did you love our baby?

66
00:03:58,000 --> 00:03:59,001
Jenphop.

67
00:04:01,411 --> 00:04:02,640
Why are you crying?

68
00:04:04,851 --> 00:04:06,160
Tell me the truth.

69
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,001
I can't do it.

70
00:04:24,568 --> 00:04:26,840
You know how much I love my children.

71
00:04:28,083 --> 00:04:29,084
I...

72
00:04:29,219 --> 00:04:30,400
I just can't do it.

73
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:34,720
A child born from an affair

74
00:04:35,347 --> 00:04:37,100
shouldn't even be considered your child.

75
00:04:39,155 --> 00:04:41,272
It's nothing but the result of your lust.

76
00:04:44,156 --> 00:04:45,400
Think carefully.

77
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:49,101
You already have two wonderful children.

78
00:04:50,915 --> 00:04:52,700
If you let that little bastard be born,

79
00:04:53,598 --> 00:04:55,600
one day Mutta will use the child to blackmail you.

80
00:04:56,568 --> 00:04:58,080
Then our family will fall apart.

81
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:02,440
Our children will hate you and stop calling you Dad.

82
00:05:02,574 --> 00:05:07,363
Your career will be ruined.

83
00:05:08,254 --> 00:05:10,760
And you can forget about the promotion I promised you.

84
00:05:12,307 --> 00:05:13,308
The whole country

85
00:05:13,502 --> 00:05:16,503
will brand you a dirty old man who preyed on a woman at work.

86
00:05:21,928 --> 00:05:23,760
Get rid of that lump of flesh.

87
00:05:25,096 --> 00:05:27,197
So you can protect the good life you have.

88
00:06:04,328 --> 00:06:06,000
I didn't want to do it, Ta.

89
00:06:08,264 --> 00:06:09,920
But Nopnapha pressured me.

90
00:06:13,387 --> 00:06:14,388
Ta.

91
00:06:17,547 --> 00:06:18,548
I'm so sorry.

92
00:06:22,072 --> 00:06:23,073
I'm sorry.

93
00:06:26,814 --> 00:06:28,250
If you still want to have a child,

94
00:06:30,798 --> 00:06:32,040
we can start over.

95
00:06:32,992 --> 00:06:33,993
Please, Ta.

96
00:06:50,358 --> 00:06:51,942
All right. Thank you.

97
00:06:54,288 --> 00:06:59,160
The airline confirmed that Jenphop and Mutta flew to Chiang Mai, ma'am.

98
00:07:01,678 --> 00:07:05,480
Find out which hotel they're staying at and their room number.

99
00:07:06,278 --> 00:07:08,250
Then book me a room nearby.

100
00:07:11,126 --> 00:07:13,800
Since I've been suspended from duty anyway,

101
00:07:14,848 --> 00:07:17,560
I might as well use my time off to give that mistress a beating.

102
00:07:17,849 --> 00:07:18,850
Ma'am.

103
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:21,521
I think going after them will only make things worse.

104
00:07:22,427 --> 00:07:23,680
Under the circumstances,

105
00:07:24,102 --> 00:07:26,800
you should keep a low profile until the scandal dies down.

106
00:07:29,278 --> 00:07:31,050
Thank you for your advice.

107
00:07:33,235 --> 00:07:34,360
But I'm not going to take it.

108
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:38,187
Brilliant! Absolutely brilliant!

109
00:07:38,304 --> 00:07:40,760
Beyond words! Simply brilliant!

110
00:09:16,326 --> 00:09:18,720
That's Director Jenphop's room.

111
00:09:22,859 --> 00:09:23,860
Your suitcase, ma'am.

112
00:09:26,188 --> 00:09:27,189
Here's your key card.

113
00:09:48,595 --> 00:09:52,760
I think you should sort out your marital problems first

114
00:09:53,171 --> 00:09:55,120
before coming back to serve the country.

115
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:03,080
So you think I'd never leave you

116
00:10:03,192 --> 00:10:05,360
and I'd spend the rest of my life begging you to stay?

117
00:10:05,816 --> 00:10:07,400
Maybe that was true before.

118
00:10:09,203 --> 00:10:10,504
But not anymore.

119
00:10:10,798 --> 00:10:12,960
Let's stop making each other miserable, Nopnapha.

120
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:14,601
Let's get a divorce.

121
00:10:25,755 --> 00:10:29,280
Before these sacred relics of the Buddha, I pray

122
00:10:29,840 --> 00:10:32,520
that all the good I've done for my country

123
00:10:32,950 --> 00:10:34,760
and all the merit I've earned

124
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:38,040
will help me overcome this crisis,

125
00:10:38,448 --> 00:10:41,640
remove those who wish me harm,

126
00:10:42,046 --> 00:10:46,080
and restore peace and happiness to my family.

127
00:10:46,090 --> 00:10:47,440
Sathu.

128
00:11:14,331 --> 00:11:16,860
What brings you to a temple, ma'am? Aren't you burning up?

129
00:11:18,272 --> 00:11:19,900
You're the one who should be burning.

130
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:23,200
Sexual misconduct.

131
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:25,640
You're having an affair with my husband, Mutta.

132
00:11:26,160 --> 00:11:27,760
Taking a life.

133
00:11:28,624 --> 00:11:29,960
And you killed my child.

134
00:11:30,496 --> 00:11:31,720
You bitch, Nopnapha!

135
00:11:33,808 --> 00:11:34,809
Get over here!

136
00:11:34,960 --> 00:11:36,520
- Come here!
- What are you doing?

137
00:11:36,939 --> 00:11:38,200
- [Wat Phra That Doi Suthep]
- Don't you dare do anything crazy!

138
00:11:38,864 --> 00:11:41,440
Do you know how many steps there are here?

139
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:46,160
306 steps.

140
00:11:47,336 --> 00:11:48,560
You've done your homework.

141
00:11:49,337 --> 00:11:51,830
Pick whichever step you want to die on.

142
00:12:32,994 --> 00:12:36,760
This is your punishment for killing me and my baby.

143
00:13:24,088 --> 00:13:25,089
Hello.

144
00:13:26,147 --> 00:13:28,960
I'm Director Jenphop Jessadaphiban's secretary.

145
00:13:29,702 --> 00:13:31,040
May I ask which room he's staying in?

146
00:13:31,302 --> 00:13:32,760
I'd like a room nearby.

147
00:13:35,430 --> 00:13:38,040
Here's my government ID.

148
00:13:39,270 --> 00:13:40,800
I really am his secretary.

149
00:13:41,238 --> 00:13:42,239
I'm not a criminal.

150
00:13:42,971 --> 00:13:46,000
Then let me call Mr. Jenphop to confirm.

151
00:13:46,235 --> 00:13:47,236
Oh, please don't.

152
00:13:47,750 --> 00:13:49,880
The director is on an important mission right now.

153
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:52,640
He gets really angry if anyone disturbs him.

154
00:13:55,101 --> 00:13:57,040
He brought a woman with him, didn't he?

155
00:13:59,300 --> 00:14:01,160
That's his mission.

156
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:07,001
Here you are.

157
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:08,041
Thank you.

158
00:14:13,840 --> 00:14:15,841
Director Jenphop must be a busy man.

159
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:17,280
He has two secretaries.

160
00:14:17,371 --> 00:14:20,400
Someone else asked for a room next to his earlier this evening.

161
00:15:10,419 --> 00:15:11,420
Excuse me.

162
00:15:11,800 --> 00:15:13,101
Do you happen to have any earplugs?

163
00:15:13,582 --> 00:15:15,560
My boss likes to watch TV with the volume turned up.

164
00:15:16,750 --> 00:15:17,760
Just a moment, please.

165
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:21,681
Here you are.

166
00:15:21,750 --> 00:15:22,751
Thank you.

167
00:15:32,424 --> 00:15:33,425
Ta.

168
00:15:35,955 --> 00:15:36,956
Aren't you...

169
00:15:37,512 --> 00:15:39,050
upstairs with Uncle Phop?

170
00:15:41,744 --> 00:15:44,400
You can see where I am. Why bother asking?

171
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:49,080
The question is, what are you doing here?

172
00:15:49,579 --> 00:15:51,280
Wait, don't answer. Let me guess.

173
00:15:52,115 --> 00:15:54,720
Oh, you're here to tell me

174
00:15:55,176 --> 00:15:57,250
you've caught me red-handed, right?

175
00:15:59,123 --> 00:16:00,720
Are you going to confess, or should I expose you?

176
00:16:01,200 --> 00:16:02,201
Don't try to trick me.

177
00:16:02,824 --> 00:16:03,825
If you know something, just say it.

178
00:16:09,838 --> 00:16:11,640
That house in Khao Yai you took Uncle Phop to see,

179
00:16:11,742 --> 00:16:13,960
where you promised you'd grow grapes together...

180
00:16:15,272 --> 00:16:16,760
That property isn't yours, is it?

181
00:16:18,462 --> 00:16:20,120
Your name isn't on the title deed.

182
00:16:20,822 --> 00:16:23,680
It belongs to someone named Munin Williams.

183
00:16:27,387 --> 00:16:28,388
Well?

184
00:16:29,286 --> 00:16:30,880
What's going through your mind?

185
00:16:32,323 --> 00:16:35,440
Trying to come up with another lie?

186
00:16:39,059 --> 00:16:40,060
No.

187
00:16:40,291 --> 00:16:42,680
Everything you said is true.

188
00:16:44,219 --> 00:16:46,700
The house in Khao Yai isn't mine.

189
00:16:47,694 --> 00:16:50,120
It belongs to my friend,  Munin.

190
00:16:50,808 --> 00:16:53,600
I just borrowed it to stage a scene and deceive your uncle.

191
00:16:54,574 --> 00:16:55,575
Deceive him?

192
00:16:57,267 --> 00:16:58,268
Why?

193
00:17:00,403 --> 00:17:02,787
It's a long story. Shall we talk at the bar?

194
00:17:08,408 --> 00:17:09,840
How did you find me here?

195
00:17:11,206 --> 00:17:12,400
And who have you been talking to?

196
00:17:13,936 --> 00:17:14,937
Titus?

197
00:17:15,835 --> 00:17:17,636
I forgot to tell her not to tell anyone.

198
00:17:18,347 --> 00:17:21,120
Does your Aunt Nopnapha know, too?

199
00:17:21,896 --> 00:17:22,960
If she wants to know,

200
00:17:23,352 --> 00:17:25,080
she has her ways of finding out.

201
00:17:27,110 --> 00:17:30,320
Her husband's run off with his mistress and isn't showing up for work.

202
00:17:30,627 --> 00:17:32,200
Of course she'd search everywhere for him.

203
00:17:36,142 --> 00:17:37,720
So, are you going to tell me the truth now?

204
00:17:39,064 --> 00:17:40,720
If I tell you the truth,

205
00:17:41,358 --> 00:17:42,360
you can't tell anyone.

206
00:17:43,075 --> 00:17:45,520
If you can't promise me that, I won't tell you.

207
00:17:47,022 --> 00:17:48,680
What if it's something illegal?

208
00:17:49,411 --> 00:17:51,880
Wouldn't that make me an accomplice?

209
00:17:53,086 --> 00:17:54,760
There's nothing illegal about it.

210
00:17:55,496 --> 00:17:58,158
Just morally wrong.

211
00:18:06,510 --> 00:18:07,511
Okay.

212
00:18:08,462 --> 00:18:09,463
Tell me.

213
00:18:13,726 --> 00:18:15,120
I don't love Director Jenphop.

214
00:18:16,419 --> 00:18:17,640
I don't want to marry him.

215
00:18:18,382 --> 00:18:20,083
I don't want to spend my life with him.

216
00:18:20,344 --> 00:18:22,787
And I don't want his money, either.

217
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:29,166
Then everything you've done...

218
00:18:30,734 --> 00:18:31,735
What's it all for?

219
00:18:33,358 --> 00:18:34,680
I'm taking revenge.

220
00:18:38,891 --> 00:18:39,892
He lied to me.

221
00:18:42,827 --> 00:18:43,828
He lied about loving me.

222
00:18:45,400 --> 00:18:47,401
He promised he'd divorce Nopnapha one day

223
00:18:47,838 --> 00:18:49,120
and marry me.

224
00:18:50,638 --> 00:18:51,960
But that day never came.

225
00:18:53,683 --> 00:18:56,250
In the end, he chose the woman who could get him promoted.

226
00:19:00,539 --> 00:19:02,120
But you're hurting Aunt Nopnapha, too, aren't you?

227
00:19:03,462 --> 00:19:04,463
What's she got to do with this?

228
00:19:05,445 --> 00:19:07,360
Nopnapha did terrible things to me, too.

229
00:19:09,800 --> 00:19:10,856
You mean

230
00:19:12,222 --> 00:19:13,750
when she slapped you and sent you tumbling down the ministry steps?

231
00:19:13,760 --> 00:19:14,799
She did far worse than that.

232
00:19:21,020 --> 00:19:22,040
I don't want to talk about it.

233
00:19:23,624 --> 00:19:25,200
But things have gone this far, Ta.

234
00:19:25,923 --> 00:19:26,924
Just tell me.

235
00:19:27,176 --> 00:19:28,480
You wouldn't believe me anyway.

236
00:19:29,718 --> 00:19:30,920
You'll find out when the time comes.

237
00:19:34,278 --> 00:19:36,360
Then what's the endgame of your revenge?

238
00:19:37,147 --> 00:19:38,320
Where does it all end?

239
00:19:41,136 --> 00:19:44,760
I can't let you keep tearing my family apart like this, Ta.

240
00:19:45,648 --> 00:19:48,760
Those two kids can barely bring themselves to go to school anymore.

241
00:19:50,158 --> 00:19:52,100
The news about their mother slapping their father

242
00:19:52,238 --> 00:19:54,120
went viral worldwide. That was your doing, wasn't it?

243
00:19:57,224 --> 00:19:58,225
At least

244
00:19:59,608 --> 00:20:00,760
you have a family to tear apart.

245
00:20:03,379 --> 00:20:04,800
I have no one left.

246
00:20:05,966 --> 00:20:07,000
Not a single person.

247
00:20:14,395 --> 00:20:16,000
I'm at the bar. Come on in.

248
00:20:21,406 --> 00:20:23,240
How did it go? Everything okay?

249
00:20:23,582 --> 00:20:25,400
All done. He's asleep.

250
00:20:26,206 --> 00:20:27,207
What about the condom?

251
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:30,240
I left it on. I didn't take it off.

252
00:20:30,971 --> 00:20:32,200
Did he see your face?

253
00:20:33,302 --> 00:20:35,040
He was drunk, and it was dark.

254
00:20:35,147 --> 00:20:36,960
He probably wouldn't have noticed if he'd slept with a pig.

255
00:20:46,070 --> 00:20:47,400
Thank you.

256
00:20:51,632 --> 00:20:53,680
Want me to take care of this one, too?

257
00:20:54,038 --> 00:20:57,050
I'll even do it for free, but let's keep the lights on.

258
00:20:57,174 --> 00:20:58,760
I want to see his face when he comes.

259
00:21:01,014 --> 00:21:02,015
I'm gay.

260
00:21:02,398 --> 00:21:03,720
I need a little gay in my system.

261
00:21:04,184 --> 00:21:05,760
Well, this gay man isn't interested in women.

262
00:21:13,080 --> 00:21:14,081
Are you serious?

263
00:21:45,934 --> 00:21:46,935
Ta.

264
00:21:49,043 --> 00:21:50,044
Ta.

265
00:22:13,880 --> 00:22:14,881
[Director Jenphop]

266
00:22:15,744 --> 00:22:16,745
I have to go.

267
00:22:16,845 --> 00:22:17,846
Excuse me.

268
00:22:18,432 --> 00:22:21,293
Please charge these two drinks to my room.

269
00:22:21,300 --> 00:22:22,301
Sure.

270
00:22:23,104 --> 00:22:25,200
I'm not treating you. Your uncle's paying.

271
00:22:25,616 --> 00:22:26,618
Wait, Ta.

272
00:22:28,486 --> 00:22:30,720
So, what are you doing tomorrow?

273
00:22:32,584 --> 00:22:34,926
Maybe I'll find a scenic spot and ask your uncle to marry me.

274
00:22:37,739 --> 00:22:38,440
Yes, Jenphop.

275
00:22:38,515 --> 00:22:40,240
I just came downstairs for a drink.

276
00:22:40,878 --> 00:22:41,920
At the bar.

277
00:22:42,632 --> 00:22:43,633
Okay.

278
00:22:50,054 --> 00:22:52,811
I missed you so much, even though we were only apart for a little while.

279
00:22:54,070 --> 00:22:55,200
Where have you been, Ta?

280
00:22:55,979 --> 00:22:57,750
Why didn't you wake me before going downstairs?

281
00:22:58,891 --> 00:23:00,760
You seemed exhausted and were fast asleep,

282
00:23:00,934 --> 00:23:02,400
so I didn't want to disturb you.

283
00:23:05,467 --> 00:23:07,712
That last round was incredible, Ta.

284
00:23:08,262 --> 00:23:10,840
Where did you learn to do that, huh?

285
00:23:11,251 --> 00:23:14,360
Your moves were so hot and unlike anything I'd ever experienced.

286
00:23:14,478 --> 00:23:18,050
I practically left my body, you know?

287
00:23:19,768 --> 00:23:22,240
I have to learn a few new tricks

288
00:23:22,435 --> 00:23:23,760
to keep you from getting bored.

289
00:23:25,894 --> 00:23:26,895
In that case,

290
00:23:28,603 --> 00:23:30,440
can we go another round like that?

291
00:23:32,651 --> 00:23:34,118
But this time, let's keep the lights on.

292
00:23:34,486 --> 00:23:35,487
Please?

293
00:23:35,782 --> 00:23:38,140
Jenphop, we have to get up early tomorrow.

294
00:23:38,406 --> 00:23:40,480
I want to explore every corner of the city.

295
00:23:40,699 --> 00:23:43,520
I haven't been here in ages. I want to see what's changed.

296
00:23:45,700 --> 00:23:48,720
What do you mean, ages? You were here last year.

297
00:23:51,254 --> 00:23:53,040
A year is a long time for me.

298
00:23:54,160 --> 00:23:56,680
Let's get some sleep. Sweet dreams.

299
00:23:59,878 --> 00:24:00,879
Ta.

300
00:24:03,222 --> 00:24:05,200
Ta, but I'm craving some khao soi.

301
00:24:05,510 --> 00:24:07,040
I need to eat it so bad.

302
00:24:07,800 --> 00:24:09,040
Go to sleep, Jenphop.

303
00:24:12,500 --> 00:24:13,501
All right, let's sleep.

304
00:24:18,190 --> 00:24:20,400
But holding you like this

305
00:24:21,840 --> 00:24:23,300
makes me happier than anything.

306
00:24:25,262 --> 00:24:28,960
I'm just as happy being in your arms, Jenphop.

307
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:48,201
It's Oshi, ma'am.

308
00:24:57,707 --> 00:24:58,708
What have you found out?

309
00:25:00,363 --> 00:25:02,600
The front desk receptionist said Jenphop rented a car

310
00:25:02,620 --> 00:25:05,200
and hired a hotel driver to take them sightseeing all day.

311
00:25:09,627 --> 00:25:11,201
And where are they now?

312
00:25:12,198 --> 00:25:13,560
Wat Phra That Doi Suthep.

313
00:25:14,920 --> 00:25:16,499
What? Where?

314
00:25:16,921 --> 00:25:19,440
Wat Phra That Doi Suthep Ratchaworawihan.

315
00:25:20,840 --> 00:25:22,696
The temple with the long staircase?

316
00:25:22,899 --> 00:25:23,900
Yes, ma'am.

317
00:25:23,976 --> 00:25:26,680
But if you don't feel like climbing, you can take the tram.

318
00:25:26,750 --> 00:25:28,050
It goes all the way to the top.

319
00:25:35,811 --> 00:25:36,812
So...

320
00:25:38,259 --> 00:25:39,480
are you going after them?

321
00:25:47,635 --> 00:25:50,320
Contact the Provincial Police Region 5 Commissioner for me.

322
00:25:51,747 --> 00:25:52,748
Yes, ma'am.

323
00:26:26,720 --> 00:26:29,160
Oshi, do you think anyone will recognize me?

324
00:26:29,846 --> 00:26:31,040
Of course not, ma'am.

325
00:26:31,050 --> 00:26:33,776
Think of all those dramas where women disguise themselves as men.

326
00:26:33,856 --> 00:26:35,371
They wear wigs and fake mustaches,

327
00:26:35,414 --> 00:26:37,201
even though they have enormous breasts.

328
00:26:37,451 --> 00:26:39,452
- They just say, Yes, sir!
- Oh!

329
00:26:39,659 --> 00:26:41,180
And nobody ever figures it out!

330
00:26:41,206 --> 00:26:42,520
You've got a point.

331
00:26:43,136 --> 00:26:44,137
Now the look is complete.

332
00:26:51,958 --> 00:26:52,959
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

333
00:26:55,190 --> 00:26:57,120
I think we should go over there. They're chanting prayers.

334
00:27:01,300 --> 00:27:02,301
Here you go.

335
00:27:08,179 --> 00:27:10,180
I swear before these sacred relics of the Buddha

336
00:27:10,728 --> 00:27:12,323
that I will marry Mutta,

337
00:27:12,995 --> 00:27:14,320
love her and her alone,

338
00:27:15,779 --> 00:27:17,320
and stay with her for the rest of my life.

339
00:27:19,923 --> 00:27:20,924
Ta.

340
00:27:21,240 --> 00:27:22,241
Will you swear the same to me?

341
00:27:24,696 --> 00:27:25,697
Yes.

342
00:27:27,331 --> 00:27:29,011
I swear

343
00:27:30,123 --> 00:27:32,118
I'll love you until the day I die.

344
00:27:33,382 --> 00:27:35,440
And if either of us breaks this vow,

345
00:27:35,784 --> 00:27:37,160
may they be damned

346
00:27:37,875 --> 00:27:39,876
and suffer agony

347
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:41,401
worse than hell on earth.

348
00:27:47,710 --> 00:27:48,711
Come on.

349
00:27:49,246 --> 00:27:50,320
I'll place the incense sticks for you.

350
00:27:54,142 --> 00:27:56,480
How intense! So passionate!

351
00:28:08,534 --> 00:28:09,535
Wow!

352
00:28:12,686 --> 00:28:13,920
What a beautiful view, Ta!

353
00:28:27,678 --> 00:28:29,579
They're making vows of eternal love, ma'am.

354
00:28:29,600 --> 00:28:31,201
Swearing to love each other until death.

355
00:28:31,296 --> 00:28:33,144
Until the end of time,

356
00:28:33,256 --> 00:28:34,960
nothing will ever separate them.

357
00:28:35,443 --> 00:28:38,080
And nothing will ever come between them.

358
00:28:39,259 --> 00:28:42,200
The director even said this is true love.

359
00:28:42,373 --> 00:28:44,360
Everything before was just a terrible mistake.

360
00:28:44,547 --> 00:28:46,320
He mistook evil for goodness,

361
00:28:46,320 --> 00:28:47,464
and worthless trash for treasure.

362
00:28:47,520 --> 00:28:48,521
Enough!

363
00:28:49,267 --> 00:28:50,268
That's enough!

364
00:28:54,622 --> 00:28:57,123
They're utterly shameless! Don't they fear divine punishment?

365
00:28:57,790 --> 00:29:00,720
How dare they make such immoral vows before a sacred shrine?

366
00:29:02,814 --> 00:29:04,400
It's time we set things right.

367
00:29:09,491 --> 00:29:10,492
Hello, ma'am.

368
00:29:10,632 --> 00:29:12,760
The commissioner sent us to assist you.

369
00:29:13,336 --> 00:29:14,337
I have two things for you to do.

370
00:29:14,680 --> 00:29:16,760
First, take my husband home.

371
00:29:17,584 --> 00:29:18,585
Second,

372
00:29:19,854 --> 00:29:21,080
do whatever it takes

373
00:29:21,750 --> 00:29:25,000
to send that mistress tumbling down the stairs

374
00:29:25,470 --> 00:29:26,960
from the very first step to the last.

375
00:29:27,758 --> 00:29:28,759
Yes, ma'am.

376
00:29:34,478 --> 00:29:36,480
Ta, why don't you look around for a bit?

377
00:29:36,787 --> 00:29:37,788
I need to use the restroom.

378
00:29:38,400 --> 00:29:39,401
Okay.

379
00:30:05,318 --> 00:30:06,518
Hey, wait!

380
00:30:06,566 --> 00:30:08,720
What the hell are you doing? Why are you arresting me?

381
00:30:08,779 --> 00:30:10,520
Hey! You're spilling it everywhere!

382
00:30:30,803 --> 00:30:33,920
You come to a temple to make merit and find peace of mind,

383
00:30:34,755 --> 00:30:36,200
but you're here with another woman's husband.

384
00:30:36,654 --> 00:30:37,920
How peaceful can your mind possibly be?

385
00:30:40,488 --> 00:30:42,760
More peaceful than someone as wicked as you,

386
00:30:44,040 --> 00:30:46,280
who could cold-bloodedly order an innocent baby killed.

387
00:30:48,360 --> 00:30:50,520
I did that child a favor.

388
00:30:51,230 --> 00:30:54,160
At least it wouldn't have to grow up with a vile mother like you.

389
00:30:57,595 --> 00:30:58,596
Ma'am.

390
00:30:59,328 --> 00:31:01,211
Please come downstairs with me.

391
00:31:02,486 --> 00:31:03,600
What gives you the right to order me around?

392
00:31:22,046 --> 00:31:23,400
You don't recognize me, do you?

393
00:31:24,211 --> 00:31:26,240
I must be pretty good at disguises!

394
00:31:27,212 --> 00:31:28,213
You stupid bitch!

395
00:31:31,360 --> 00:31:32,880
[Wat Phra That Doi Suthep Ratchaworawihan]

396
00:31:45,344 --> 00:31:46,560
You've been sleeping with my husband

397
00:31:47,510 --> 00:31:49,750
and living off my money long enough.

398
00:31:50,907 --> 00:31:52,840
It's time for you to fall from grace, Mutta.

399
00:31:53,480 --> 00:31:54,481
In hell,

400
00:31:54,939 --> 00:31:56,640
you can sleep around all you want,

401
00:31:57,171 --> 00:31:59,240
because that's where scum like you belong.

402
00:32:01,070 --> 00:32:02,071
Let her go.

403
00:32:04,878 --> 00:32:08,250
I'll personally send you straight to the depths of hell.

404
00:32:09,195 --> 00:32:11,880
Do you know how many steps there are here?

405
00:32:17,000 --> 00:32:18,160
306 steps.

406
00:32:18,848 --> 00:32:19,920
You've done your homework.

407
00:32:21,174 --> 00:32:23,880
Now pick which step you want to die on.

408
00:32:35,486 --> 00:32:37,920
Hatred is never ended by hatred.

409
00:32:42,454 --> 00:32:43,920
This is a place of compassion.

410
00:32:44,683 --> 00:32:46,880
Please, I beg you to spare her.

411
00:32:47,544 --> 00:32:49,280
You may be able to shut down every camera in this temple

412
00:32:49,763 --> 00:32:51,320
and suppress the news throughout the city,

413
00:32:51,630 --> 00:32:54,280
but you cannot silence your own conscience.

414
00:32:54,643 --> 00:32:56,400
If you push her down those stairs,

415
00:32:57,115 --> 00:33:00,779
you'll sink even lower than she does.

416
00:33:08,256 --> 00:33:09,920
Your good karma has saved you this time.

417
00:33:11,942 --> 00:33:14,943
You're lucky the monk came to your rescue.

418
00:33:16,360 --> 00:33:17,560
You must have plenty of merit left.

419
00:33:18,878 --> 00:33:20,280
But once your luck runs out,

420
00:33:20,678 --> 00:33:22,000
I'll make sure you die.

421
00:33:26,216 --> 00:33:27,417
Goodbye, Venerable Sir.

422
00:33:41,808 --> 00:33:43,120
Thank you, Venerable Sir.

423
00:33:43,536 --> 00:33:44,960
The same goes for you, my child.

424
00:33:45,606 --> 00:33:47,440
The sooner you learn to let go,

425
00:33:47,982 --> 00:33:50,200
the sooner your heart will find peace.

426
00:33:51,000 --> 00:33:52,720
If someone murdered your younger sister,

427
00:33:53,160 --> 00:33:56,280
would you let go and allow the killer to walk free?

428
00:33:56,776 --> 00:33:57,880
In Buddhist teachings,

429
00:33:58,246 --> 00:33:59,472
letting go

430
00:33:59,563 --> 00:34:01,472
means releasing your attachment to suffering

431
00:34:01,675 --> 00:34:03,862
and the hatred you carry.

432
00:34:04,864 --> 00:34:06,100
But in the secular world,

433
00:34:06,544 --> 00:34:09,840
we must allow the law to take its course.

434
00:34:10,339 --> 00:34:13,800
Unfortunately, this killer happens to be above the law.

435
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:15,001
You saw it yourself.

436
00:34:15,155 --> 00:34:16,910
She was about to throw me down the stairs.

437
00:34:17,288 --> 00:34:19,160
If the law cannot bring her to justice,

438
00:34:19,685 --> 00:34:23,120
trust that the law of karma is always just.

439
00:34:23,766 --> 00:34:24,767
Then I'll be

440
00:34:25,275 --> 00:34:26,360
her karma

441
00:34:27,109 --> 00:34:28,360
and deliver her punishment myself.

442
00:34:30,939 --> 00:34:32,320
Farewell, Venerable Sir.

443
00:34:35,766 --> 00:34:37,500
But you paid no heed.

444
00:34:44,000 --> 00:34:45,001
Nopnapha.

445
00:34:48,915 --> 00:34:51,843
You're getting closer to becoming a criminal every day.

446
00:34:53,022 --> 00:34:55,880
I was a criminal long before I became a politician. You know that.

447
00:34:57,165 --> 00:34:58,240
So what are you going to do to me?

448
00:34:58,491 --> 00:34:59,960
Burn me alive in a tire?

449
00:35:00,070 --> 00:35:02,840
Go on, bring me a tire! I'll sit in it!

450
00:35:03,547 --> 00:35:05,320
I just want to take you home.

451
00:35:06,387 --> 00:35:10,240
You can't go parading around the country with your mistress like this!

452
00:35:11,747 --> 00:35:13,200
Never forget

453
00:35:13,300 --> 00:35:16,170
that you're Minister Nopnapha's husband.

454
00:35:16,758 --> 00:35:18,059
Show me some respect and stop humiliating me.

455
00:35:18,159 --> 00:35:20,000
You've never cared about my dignity, either.

456
00:35:20,248 --> 00:35:22,192
There's a simple solution.

457
00:35:22,443 --> 00:35:24,920
Let's get divorced and go our separate ways.

458
00:35:25,059 --> 00:35:27,060
Then neither of us will have to worry about saving face anymore.

459
00:35:27,342 --> 00:35:28,343
Okay?

460
00:35:29,470 --> 00:35:30,471
Drive.

461
00:35:35,567 --> 00:35:36,650
Hey, Nopnapha!

462
00:35:36,712 --> 00:35:38,050
Are you even listening to me?

463
00:35:39,471 --> 00:35:40,472
Nopnapha!

464
00:35:41,792 --> 00:35:42,793
Hey!

465
00:35:43,221 --> 00:35:44,789
What's with the disguise?

466
00:35:45,461 --> 00:35:46,462
Oh!

467
00:35:46,762 --> 00:35:48,090
You recognized me, Director?

468
00:35:48,167 --> 00:35:49,910
And here I thought my disguise was perfect.

469
00:35:49,930 --> 00:35:51,460
Of course I recognize you.

470
00:35:51,671 --> 00:35:53,220
You're Joey Ghana!

471
00:35:53,500 --> 00:35:54,501
Can you even speak Thai?

472
00:35:54,556 --> 00:35:56,320
I speak it better than your father!

473
00:35:59,695 --> 00:36:01,140
You cheeky bastard!

474
00:36:02,120 --> 00:36:03,220
Want me to give you a beating?

475
00:36:21,270 --> 00:36:22,271
Ta.

476
00:36:28,546 --> 00:36:29,547
Are you okay?

477
00:36:31,128 --> 00:36:33,210
Why are you alone? Where's Uncle Phop?

478
00:36:33,858 --> 00:36:35,290
His wife had him dragged back home.

479
00:36:35,506 --> 00:36:36,890
He just texted me.

480
00:36:38,904 --> 00:36:39,905
So,

481
00:36:41,256 --> 00:36:42,370
what are you going to do now?

482
00:36:46,649 --> 00:36:47,670
I'm craving some khao soi.

483
00:37:59,153 --> 00:38:00,154
Let's take some pictures.

484
00:38:00,740 --> 00:38:01,741
Come on.

485
00:38:02,055 --> 00:38:03,056
Ta, go stand over there.

486
00:38:12,956 --> 00:38:13,980
Could you at least smile?

487
00:38:14,812 --> 00:38:15,980
Why are you so upset?

488
00:38:24,859 --> 00:38:26,260
Let's go somewhere else. Come on.

489
00:40:03,230 --> 00:40:04,231
What's wrong?

490
00:40:04,473 --> 00:40:05,474
Come on, smile.

491
00:40:08,230 --> 00:40:09,231
I don't feel like smiling.

492
00:40:12,434 --> 00:40:13,435
How about this?

493
00:40:14,184 --> 00:40:15,210
Let's flip a coin.

494
00:40:15,986 --> 00:40:17,730
If it's tails, you have to smile.

495
00:40:18,317 --> 00:40:20,890
If it's heads, I'll jump into the water.

496
00:40:21,469 --> 00:40:22,470
Deal?

497
00:40:23,650 --> 00:40:24,651
You'll really jump?

498
00:40:24,813 --> 00:40:26,050
Of course!

499
00:40:27,954 --> 00:40:29,890
Fine. If it's tails, I'll smile.

500
00:40:30,210 --> 00:40:31,211
If it's heads, you jump.

501
00:40:32,314 --> 00:40:33,690
- You promise?
- Yeah.

502
00:40:39,248 --> 00:40:40,249
Tails.

503
00:40:46,197 --> 00:40:47,198
Tails.

504
00:40:47,370 --> 00:40:48,371
Now smile!

505
00:40:49,480 --> 00:40:50,481
Come on, smile!

506
00:40:51,229 --> 00:40:52,230
Let's see.

507
00:40:52,397 --> 00:40:53,398
Let me see.

508
00:41:01,626 --> 00:41:03,250
Both sides are tails!

509
00:41:04,245 --> 00:41:05,410
You cheated!

510
00:41:06,416 --> 00:41:07,417
Hey, Ta.

511
00:41:08,330 --> 00:41:09,331
That's a rare coin!

512
00:41:10,135 --> 00:41:12,050
Wait! You haven't thrown it yet!

513
00:41:12,450 --> 00:41:13,451
Here it is.

514
00:41:15,142 --> 00:41:17,240
You scared me! Do you know how rare that coin is?

515
00:41:18,326 --> 00:41:20,880
What kind of magician falls for such an old trick?

516
00:41:21,291 --> 00:41:22,292
Amateur!

517
00:41:22,934 --> 00:41:23,935
Give it back.

518
00:41:38,804 --> 00:41:40,150
When you were lost in thought just now,

519
00:41:41,468 --> 00:41:43,540
you looked like the old Mutta again. You know that?

520
00:41:47,116 --> 00:41:48,117
Really?

521
00:41:48,626 --> 00:41:49,627
How?

522
00:41:50,519 --> 00:41:51,660
You used to stare off into space,

523
00:41:52,775 --> 00:41:53,860
looking so sad.

524
00:41:59,452 --> 00:42:00,460
Did I do that a lot?

525
00:42:04,636 --> 00:42:05,637
Yeah.

526
00:42:06,145 --> 00:42:08,178
But ever since you said you were going to become a new person,

527
00:42:08,983 --> 00:42:10,420
I haven't seen that look in your eyes again.

528
00:42:11,820 --> 00:42:12,821
Until just now.

529
00:42:26,868 --> 00:42:28,554
So which version of me do you like better?

530
00:42:30,183 --> 00:42:31,420
The old me or the new me?

531
00:42:34,743 --> 00:42:36,660
The one standing right in front of me, of course.

532
00:42:42,852 --> 00:42:44,180
That's why I want you to smile.

533
00:42:46,207 --> 00:42:47,340
You seem more alive.

534
00:42:52,370 --> 00:42:53,740
But you're also a lot more trouble.

535
00:42:54,759 --> 00:42:55,760
You're exhausting.

536
00:42:57,378 --> 00:42:58,740
That's some seriously negative positivity.

537
00:42:59,628 --> 00:43:01,740
Can't you just give me a compliment? Why do you always have to ruin it?

538
00:43:01,807 --> 00:43:03,320
You've ruined such a lovely moment!

539
00:43:03,497 --> 00:43:04,620
Whoa, someone's throwing a tantrum!

540
00:43:04,670 --> 00:43:06,700
I should've left you at the temple for the monk to straighten out.

541
00:43:06,740 --> 00:43:07,980
Even the monk got an earful from me.

542
00:43:08,772 --> 00:43:09,773
Huh?

543
00:43:10,575 --> 00:43:11,700
You yelled at a monk?

544
00:43:12,890 --> 00:43:13,891
Yeah.

545
00:43:13,946 --> 00:43:15,060
Wow, Ta!

546
00:43:15,861 --> 00:43:17,340
You're a menace to Buddhism.

547
00:43:18,719 --> 00:43:19,820
If that's what you think, take this back.

548
00:43:21,471 --> 00:43:22,580
No returns, sorry.

549
00:43:32,864 --> 00:43:35,240
There you are again! Everywhere I go, I run into you.

550
00:43:35,386 --> 00:43:36,387
Are you stalking me?

551
00:43:52,551 --> 00:43:53,552
Nina?

552
00:43:54,346 --> 00:43:55,347
Finally.

553
00:43:55,380 --> 00:43:56,820
Hey! Step back!

554
00:43:57,348 --> 00:43:58,349
Don't touch her.

555
00:43:58,895 --> 00:43:59,940
She's my girlfriend.

556
00:44:00,260 --> 00:44:01,261
Tell him, Nina.

557
00:44:22,740 --> 00:44:24,980
If you're afraid of the humiliation of divorcing your husband,

558
00:44:25,114 --> 00:44:28,460
I'll make you even more humiliated for refusing to divorce me.

559
00:44:28,588 --> 00:44:30,100
Do you two really love each other?

560
00:44:30,279 --> 00:44:31,820
Jenphop loves me very much.

561
00:44:32,444 --> 00:44:34,280
But I don't love him one bit.

562
00:44:34,482 --> 00:44:36,580
I want him to divorce you

563
00:44:37,154 --> 00:44:38,300
just for the satisfaction of it.

564
00:44:38,820 --> 00:44:40,860
It's purely for my own amusement.

565
00:44:41,780 --> 00:44:44,420
Nopnapha's about to unveil her Smart Card project. Hurry!

566
00:44:44,466 --> 00:44:48,940
Mrs.Nopnapha Jessadaphiban is showing signs of mental instability.

567
00:44:49,487 --> 00:44:52,380
It's like a completely different AI from the one we trained!

568
00:44:53,680 --> 00:44:54,681
Munin.

569
00:44:55,098 --> 00:44:56,695
Would you like to serve your country

570
00:44:57,178 --> 00:44:59,700
by getting rid of a corrupt politician and making her die of rage?

571
00:44:59,980 --> 00:45:01,820
Ta, what do you want me to do?

572
00:45:03,650 --> 00:45:04,651
Nina?
